                                Dots in Fig. 12 show the maximum number of spans n as a function of
                            the order of QAM m, when POLMUX ﬁve WDM channels are transmitted.
                            We ﬁnd that n is inversely proportional to m as seen from the solid line and
                            that transmission distances of 64 QAM and 256 QAM systems are severely
                            limited below 1,000 km. Thus, when we aim at higher spectral eﬃciency
                            with higher-order QAM, the performance of such system will strongly be re-
                            stricted by ﬁber nonlinearity. Although the back-propagation method was
                            proposed to compensate for ﬁber nonlinearity [38, 39], huge computational
                            complexity prevents its practical application. Finding practical countermea-
                            sure against ﬁber nonlinearity is one of the most crucial issues in coherent
                            optical communication systems.

                            7 Future prospects

                            The progress of digital coherent technologies is very rapid. However, the
                            following is the technical problems that must be tackled and accomplished

                                                                                                                                                               1660
